// The rule inventory: every rule the agent-team guidance holds, once.
//
// Each entry is [id, home, anchor, rule, enforced?]:
//   id        stable name; the prefix says which file family it lives in
//   home      the ONE file that states the rule (the rest point at it)
//   anchor    a short regex that must match the home file. It is a presence
//             check, not a wording pin: keep it to a few distinctive words.
//   rule      the rule in plain words (this text is the inventory)
//   enforced  what makes it hold besides the words: 'guard', 'merge-task',
//             'ci-wait', 'logger', 'handback-check', or absent (words only)
//
// tests/guidance.test.js checks every anchor, and docs/guidance.md says how to
// add, move or drop a rule. Rewording a file is free as long as the anchors
// still match; removing a rule means removing its entry here, on purpose.
